For the following elemental reaction steps indicate the molecularity and give the rate law:
\begin{inparaenum}[(a)]
\item \ce{SiH4 + SiH2 -> Si2H6 }   %molecularity=2; $r$=k[\ce{SiH2}][\ce{SiH4}]
\item \ce{SiH2 + H -> SiH + H2 }   %molecularity=2; $r$=k[\ce{SiH2}][\ce{H}]
\item \ce{Si2H3 + H2 -> Si2H5 }   %molecularity=2; $r$=k[\ce{Si2H3}][\ce{H2}]
\end{inparaenum}
